<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27264" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διόρθ-ωσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>making straight,</i> as in the setting of a limb, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Off.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mochl.</u>
				38
			</span></i>; <i>setting straight, restoration,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκοδομημάτων καὶ ὁδῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1321b21
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>correction, chastisement,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ διορθώσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.56.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διορθώσεως σφίσι δεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					6.20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>amendment, correction,</i> of men, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				7.11.2
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1317a35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.118.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν νόμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					9(1).694.137
				</span></i>
			 (Corc.); <i>correction,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρωτημάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>SE</u>
					176b34
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1275a20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς δ. ἄγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.58.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ.,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλάβη,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.88.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orib.
					5.4
				</span></i>
			 tit. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>right treatment,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					642a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>recension, revised edition of</i> a work, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.397
			</span></i>: in pl., <i>emendations,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				3.66
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>payment,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀψωνίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.50.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				61
			</span></i> (<i>a</i>). <i><span class="en">
				33
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
